State whether each study is cross-sectional, retrospective, or prospective.  

a) To see if there is a link between smoking and bladder cancer, patients with bladder cancer are asked if they currently smoke or if they smoked in the past.  
b) The Nurses Health Survey was a survey where nurses were asked to record their eating habits over a period of time, and their general health was recorded.  
c) A new study is underway to track the eating and exercise patterns of people at different time-periods in the future, and see who is afflicted with cancer later in life.  
d) The prices of generic items are compared to the prices of the equivalent named brand items.
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The study types are as follows:  
a) **retrospective** – The study looks backward to the past (e.g., past smoking habits) to identify potential risk factors for a disease (bladder cancer).  
b) **prospective** – The study follows a group of nurses over time to observe changes in their eating habits and health.  
c) **prospective** – The study tracks participants forward in time to see who develops cancer, based on their current eating and exercise habits.  
d) **cross-sectional** – The study compares prices at a single point in time (e.g., right now).  

**Key Differences:**  
- **Cross-sectional**: Data is collected at one point in time.  
- **Retrospective**: Looks backward in time to examine past events and their potential effects.  
- **Prospective**: Follows subjects forward in time to observe future outcomes.  

$\boxed{\text{The study types are as follows:  
a) retrospective, b) prospective, c) prospective, d) cross-sectional.}}$
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

