Distance a travels in 3 hours = speed × time = 10 kmph × 3 hours = 30 km.
When b starts cycling, a is already 30 km away from the start.
Now, b cycles at 20 kmh, and a continues to walk at 10 kmh.
The relative speed of b with respect to a is the difference in their speeds, since b is moving in the same direction as a.
Relative speed = 20 kmph - 10 kmph = 10 kmph.
The time taken for b to catch up with a is the distance a is away from the start when b starts, divided by the relative speed.
Time taken for b to catch up with a = distance / relative speed = 30 km / 10 kmph = 3 hours.
